course: dictionary
lesson: 15591
title: Tableware and the things we eat from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tableware is a noun for all the things we use to serve and eat a meal at a table: plates, bowls, cups, glasses, knives, forks and spoons. It is a group word, like furniture or clothing. «We bought new party tableware for the birthday tea.» The words around tableware show you it is for a party, and you can picture bright paper plates and cups.
explain: Tableware is uncountable, so you never say «two tablewares» or «a tableware». You say «some tableware» or «a set of tableware». To count the things, name them: two plates, three cups, four forks. «The museum had Roman tableware made of clay.» Here the clue is museum: old things, made long ago, kept for us to look at.
explain: Shops, history lessons and home all use this word. In a shop it is in the kitchen section. In design and technology you might study tableware from different times. At home, when you help set the table, you are laying out the tableware. Look for «tableware» in these places and the meaning will stick.
fact: Tableware means all the things used for serving and eating a meal at a table.
fact: Tableware includes plates, bowls, cups, glasses, knives, forks and spoons.
fact: Tableware is uncountable: say «some tableware», not «two tablewares».
fact: «Plastic tableware» means dishes and cutlery made of plastic, often for picnics or parties.
fact: «Fine tableware» means good-quality, special dishes and cups, often kept for important meals.
exercise: «Please set the table with the tableware.» What is tableware? | A kind of cupboard for shoes | *Things used for serving and eating a meal, like plates and forks | A wooden table with four legs | A tray for carrying the post
exercise: Which of these is tableware? | A garden hose | *A plate for your dinner | A pair of trainers | A tennis racket
exercise: What word in «The museum had Roman tableware made of clay.» names dishes used for eating a meal? | *tableware | clay | Roman | Museum
test: Which of these is a kind of tableware? | A cookery book | A bicycle bell | A desk lamp | *A wine glass
test: What does «fine tableware» suggest? | Dirty dishes left in the sink | Garden tools | Cheap plastic plates for picnics | *Good-quality, special dishes and cups
exam: Which phrase is correct? | two tablewares | *some tableware | a tableware | three tablewares
